The inference edit fuses each chamfer translation into the bilinear sample so stage 2 still poses only the pallet `select_detection` already chose.

`chamfer_cost_from_rotated` was copying the rotated contour into `tls.translated` on every grid step, then sampling that copy. It now reads the rotated x and y columns, adds `tx` and `ty` in the sample loop, and keeps the same ascending trimmed mean. The search still calls that cost once per translation, not once per extra detection.

The behavior test failed first because that copy was still there. After the change, `python geometry_core/test/test_fused_chamfer_sample.py` reported 2 tests, OK. The command is in `runs/Absolute_2026-09-28_02/workers/cycle-001/edit-result-inference_edit.json`.
